From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PatchForge
Date: Sat, 6 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Windows compat: POSIX-style rel_fname in RepoGraph

On Windows, os.path.relpath yields backslash separators
(e.g. docs\_themes\file.py), but get_tags_raw looks the path up in
the structure dict via rel_fname.split('/'), raising KeyError for any
file in a subdirectory. Observed on psf/requests @ a0df2cb:
KeyError: 'docs\\_themes\\flask_theme_support.py'.

Fix: normalize to forward slashes in get_rel_fname. No-op on Linux
(os.sep == '/'). All downstream uses (tag fields, to_tree grouping,
jsonl/pkl output) are string-level and match Linux behavior.

Apply from the RepoGraph clone root:
  git apply <workspace>/patches/repograph-windows-paths.patch

Revert:
  git -C third_party/RepoGraph checkout -- repograph/construct_graph.py

Upstream status: not fixed upstream as of 2026-09-06.
Do NOT commit into third_party/; this file is the record (§24).

--- a/repograph/construct_graph.py
+++ b/repograph/construct_graph.py
@@ -113,7 +113,9 @@
         return G
 
     def get_rel_fname(self, fname):
-        return os.path.relpath(fname, self.root)
+        # POSIX-style separators: downstream lookup splits on '/'
+        # (KeyError on Windows otherwise). No-op on Linux.
+        return os.path.relpath(fname, self.root).replace(os.sep, "/")
 
     def split_path(self, path):
         path = os.path.relpath(path, self.root)
